# round 36 (w52): the layer-free log1p form over a store built by another solver. The solve read (sec:solve-tolerance) found the program's argmax degenerate and a probe fitted within the interior point as rankable as the vertex; this is the training test. The same growth-maximizing program (the round-27 one, no parsimony stage) solved per gene by HiGHS's dual simplex (a vertex; pathlogsimplex) and by its interior point without crossover at KKT 1e-4 (a point inside the optimal face, the kind a first-order solve on the card returns; pathlogipm), each store read by the round-33 cell (log1p, default init, pathway + ProtT5, no layer). Paired by seed against w49_pathfbapfbalogfree (the pFBA store). ESS_SOLVE_TABLE points the trainer at the store. Six seeds each, pooled cells, ESS_MEM=72g ESS_CPUS=12
ESS_SOLVE_TABLE=/scratch/projects/torchcell-scratch/data/torchcell/reference_flux/ess_solve_encodings_YPD_simplex.npz ESS_ARM=pooled ESS_HIDDEN=12 ESS_HEADS=4 ESS_LAYERS=1 ESS_PREPROC=1 ESS_EPOCHS=200 ESS_BATCH=32 ESS_POSW=1 ESS_SPLIT=ess_fcl_val0.2_s0.json.gz ESS_SEED=2700 ESS_TAG=_w52pathlogsimplex ESS_OUT=w52_pathlogsimplex_h12l1p1_e200_s2700 ESS_EXTRA='--node-embeddings pathways prot_T5_all --ess-readout fba --ess-solve-features pfba --ess-solve-encoding log1p'
